WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Next up some news from another woman who breaks the mold,

2
00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:06.830
the endlessly talented Jenny Slate.

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.850
She is one of my favorite people.

4
00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.180
And I'm happy to report

5
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.840
that it's time to fire up those tear ducts

6
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.960
because "Marcel The Shell,"

7
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.650
the famous character that she created is getting a movie.

8
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.770
Jenny is bringing the little shell to the big screen,

9
00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:25.320
that she created with Dean Fleischer-Camp

10
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.530
in the Director's seat.

11
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.610
And they created Marcel together a decade ago.

12
00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.880
Please take a look at this.

13
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.390
Sometimes I find my mind wandering,

14
00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.153
thinking, what would my family think?

15
00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:40.429
(rain trickling)

16
00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:42.133
Do you think they could be out there?

17
00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:47.400
Marcelo, let's forget about being afraid,

18
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.608
just take the adventure.

19
00:00:49.608 --> 00:00:52.104
Okay Lyn, let's do it.

20
00:00:52.104 --> 00:00:52.937
(audience applauding)

21
00:00:52.937 --> 00:00:55.290
Oh my god, he's so sweet.

22
00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.600
I cannot wait.

23
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.040
I'm not kidding, I have chills everywhere.

24
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.610
And guess what?

25
00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:04.931
On the phone right now we've got "Marcel The Shell."

26
00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:08.098
(audience applauding)

27
00:01:10.206 --> 00:01:12.770
Hi guys.
Oh it's actually

28
00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:13.603
Jenny Slate.

29
00:01:13.603 --> 00:01:14.491
Hi, it's Jenny.

30
00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:15.581
Jenny Slate.

31
00:01:15.581 --> 00:01:16.414
Hi Jenny.

32
00:01:17.949 --> 00:01:19.109 line:15%
Oh, I love Jenny.

33
00:01:19.109 --> 00:01:19.942 line:15%
Hi guys.

34
00:01:19.942 --> 00:01:21.651 line:15%
Oh Jenny.
Hi guys.

35
00:01:21.651 --> 00:01:22.484 line:15%
I love you so much.

36
00:01:22.484 --> 00:01:24.930 line:15%
Thank you so much for coming on this show.

37
00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:27.950 line:15%
I've been texting you night and day.

38
00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:32.120 line:15%
Is it like true that Marcel might be the closest

39
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.810 line:15%
to your (indistinct) center?

40
00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:36.040 line:15%
Yeah, I will say that, you know

41
00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.100 line:15%
Marcel and the way he is

42
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.390 line:15%
and his easy confidence

43
00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:42.610 line:15%
and his immediate connection to things

44
00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:44.117 line:15%
that are really beautiful and important.

45
00:01:44.117 --> 00:01:45.780 line:15%
Maybe it's not like,

46
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:49.210 line:15%
I think it's like closest to what I aspire to be like,

47
00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.200 line:15%
you know to like it's like closest to my best self and,

48
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.840 line:15%
that's why he's a great character to perform

49
00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.780 line:15%
because I get to step into that mode

50
00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:58.910 line:15%
and the more I step into it

51
00:01:58.910 --> 00:02:00.970 line:15%
the more I can replicate it in my own life.

52
00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.520 line:15%
And I think that's just a huge privilege.

53
00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:06.333 line:15%
Do you think that Marcel could come to the phone?

54
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:07.952 line:15%
(laughing)

55
00:02:07.952 --> 00:02:09.550
Oh yeah.

56
00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:12.480
Marcel, you are on the big screen.

57
00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:16.880
What do you hope that people will take away from this movie?

58
00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.267 line:15%
I guess I just want everyone to know that,

59
00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.550 line:15%
it's not only about me because I'm extraordinary,

60
00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:31.110 line:15%
but because actually everybody has an interesting story

61
00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:34.440 line:15%
if we just take the time to get know them

62
00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:37.462 line:15%
and let them be comfortable enough to be themselves.

63
00:02:37.462 --> 00:02:40.761 line:15%
So, I guess I'm trying be modest also.

64
00:02:40.761 --> 00:02:43.700 line:15%
(indistinct)

65
00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:44.783 line:15%
Aw.

66
00:02:45.975 --> 00:02:47.682 line:15%
(audience applauding)

67
00:02:47.682 --> 00:02:49.482 line:15%
You're right, Marcel.

68
00:02:49.482 --> 00:02:50.354 line:15%
You are right.

69
00:02:50.354 --> 00:02:55.354
We are all gonna get into the groove with you

70
00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.740
and Jenny Slate.

71
00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:01.960
One of my favorite minds and hearts out there.

72
00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:05.320
I mean, Jenny as a writer I love you,

73
00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:06.800
as an actress I love you,

74
00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.250
as a comedian I love you,

75
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:14.200
and obviously I love "Marcel The Shell With Shoes On,"

76
00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:17.510
comes out in theater's June 24th.

77
00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.760
Be aware, get it while it's hot.

78
00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.482 line:15%
And Marcel has had a lot to teach us over the last decade.

79
00:03:23.482 --> 00:03:26.630 line:15%
And it's definitely a good thing

80
00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.110
that he has his own movie,

81
00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.645
so that we can all continue

82
00:03:29.645 --> 00:03:31.917
to love and learn from Marcel.

83
00:03:31.917 --> 00:03:33.770
Marcel the movie star.

84
00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:36.353 line:15%
(upbeat music)

